'' 'len( mod.F( ) )' BINDS THE MODULE'S F. fbc drops a NAMESPACE prefix inside len, sizeof
'' and typeof (resolveintr.tiko DropNsPrefix_), and that quirk was applied to an imported
'' module too, which fbc has no notion of: 'len( dates.CurrentDate( ) )' was TKO0743 or
'' an ICE where a bare name of that spelling was in view (tracks-2026 TB-006). A global
'' 'Num( ) as short' sits beside the module's long one to show which is measured.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/lenmod/libs tests/modules/src/lenmod/app/main.tiko -o tests/modules/lenmodlink.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/modules/lenmodlink.exe
'' RUN: tests/modules/lenmodlink.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  10
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  70000
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  10
